  "fields": [
    {
      "entryId": "1jn-3-8",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "For this purpose the Son of God was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil. Textual proof: Genesis 3:15 — seed of the woman crushes the serpent; Col 2:15; Heb 2:14 — destroy him that had the power of death.",
      "density": 2.5036,
      "words": 43,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 25,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": [
          "Genesis 3:15",
          "Colossians 2:15",
          "Hebrews 2:14"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1jn-3-2",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Now sons; then like Him at the appearing. First principle: vision transforms — the sight of Him as He is is the mechanism of likeness; hope purifies in the meantime.",
      "density": 2.1571,
      "words": 30,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 22,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1jn-2-1",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Sin-not writing with a sin-answer. First principle: the Advocate is the Righteous One pleading — the courtroom of heaven has a defense attorney whose argument is His own righteousness.",
      "density": 2.0964,
      "words": 29,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 24,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1jn-4-10",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Love defined from God's side. First principle: love is not our initiative but His sending — propitiation is the definition of divine love, not an aftermath of it.",
      "density": 2.0143,
      "words": 28,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 23,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1jn-2-2",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Propitiation beyond the letter's readers. First principle: the wrath-removing sacrifice is sufficient for the world — the mercy-seat term (hilasmos) from Leviticus 16 applied to the cross.",
      "density": 1.9321,
      "words": 27,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 22,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1jn-5-6",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Not water only — water and blood, with the Spirit witnessing. First principle: the double testimony answers the docetic denial — the Son came through real baptism and real blood.",
      "density": 1.8357,
      "words": 30,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1jn-5-8",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Spirit, water, blood — agreeing in one. First principle: the legal standard of two-or-three witnesses is met by a triple testimony; heaven's case is established on earth.",
      "density": 1.8179,
      "words": 27,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 20,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1jn-4-9",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Manifested love so we might live through Him. First principle: love is measured by the gift's cost and the recipient's death — sent Son, living receivers.",
      "density": 1.6786,
      "words": 26,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 18,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1jn-1-1",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The Word of life — heard, seen, looked upon, handled. First principle: the incarnation is forensic — apostolic senses are the witnesses; the eternal Word became touchable.",
      "density": 1.6464,
      "words": 27,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 17,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "1jn-3-12",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Cain's murder explained: evil works, righteous brother. First principle: the first murder was worship-envy — the wicked one's children still hate righteousness's presence.",
      "density": 1.4893,
      "words": 23,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 16,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
